{
  "_source": "UHV-A1 (docs/eras/uhv.md, 'A1. Transcurium', machines 1 and 2, lines 1-3 and 25): the recipes of UHV's high flux reactor and transuranium facility, and the GTM chemical reactor rows of line 25. Real processes: ORNL's HFIR (a flux trap at 2.5e15 n/cm2.s; curium and americium-243 targets bred to berkelium-249 and californium-252; nickel-62 to nickel-63) and REDC (targets dissolved in nitric acid, the actinides split by HDEHP extraction and cation exchange; the Bk-249 shipped for tennessine in 2009); thorium-229 milked from aged uranium-233 (ORNL, Karlsruhe); HDEHP made from 2-ethylhexanol (the oxo and aldol route from propene) and phosphoryl chloride.",
  "_how_it_is_used": [
    "Read by server_scripts/grindless/uhv/transcurium.js at every server load. Each entry of types.<type>.recipes becomes one gtceu:<type> recipe, id grindless:<type>/<name>, carrying the data key of its type = <name> (its EMI line, gtceu.recipe.<dataKey>.<name>).",
    "itemsIn / itemsOut: { id, count }; fluidsIn / fluidsOut: { id, amount } in mB; kept: items never used up (GTM notConsumable); charge: fluids never used up (notConsumableFluid). eut x duration.",
    "The programmed circuit picks the recipe: one per recipe inside a type (1-32). chemical_reactor rows may carry a circuit (0 = none) so GTM's own chemical reactor recipes cannot hide them.",
    "Loops: the drivers come from IV's fuel fabrication plant (tables/transcurium_fabrication.json) and go back as uranium-233 through UV's pyroprocessing cell (tables/transcurium_pyroprocessing.json). The heavy curium oxide of separate goes into the next target. The decay store's 8 uranium-233 come back whole. The HDEHP solvent comes back less 1 %; the spent part is incinerated to phosphoric acid. The nitric acid of the raffinate and of the evaporator comes back.",
    "Destinations: radioactive waste (activated cladding, the evaporated fission products) -> ZPM's waste retrieval plant (synroc); berkelium-249 is stored for UEV; californium-252 -> the reactor's circuit 3 (sealed sources); nickel-63 targets -> the betavoltaic line; thorium-229 -> the nuclear clock line; HCl of the HDEHP step -> GTM's HCl uses; water of the aldol step and of the incinerator -> anywhere; CO2 of the incinerator -> GTM's CO2 uses."
  ],
